      "text": "Tech stocks tumbled for the second day in a row as concerns rise over the hundreds of billions of dollars they are investing in artificial intelligence (AI).\nShares in Intel plummeted by as much as 30% following Google owner Alphabet's stock price plunging by more than $500bn in the previous day's trading.\nOther tech stocks including Reddit and Amazon also fell while the Nasdaq index of the largest tech firms listed in the US sank over 3.5%.\nWhile tech firms as spending big on AI, some of their earnings are not meeting analysts' expectations, spooking investors and creating fears about a potential AI bubble.\nMajor tech companies have ramped up artificial intelligence spending, with Meta, Alphabet, Oracle, Amazon, and Microsoft committing $800.6bn between them in this year alone.\nAlphabet's stock market value plunged on Thursday after it revealed its own AI summaries were affecting its core search advertising revenue.\nAt the same time, Alphabet expects to spend up to $205bn this year on investments, almost entirely related to AI.\nAlphabet stock continued to fall in early trading, down 1% after Thursday's massive slide.\nThe bigger losses on Friday were elsewhere, with Intel on track to lose more than $130bn in value as its shares continued to fall in Friday trading.\nThe chip maker said it planned to increase spending on AI despite weaker demand for computers, rattling investors.\nOn Thursday, Intel's finance chief David Zinsner said the firm did not expect to bring in more cash than it spent this year, and forecast lower-than-expected revenue for its fourth quarter.\n\"Looking ahead, we see the PC slowdown continuing at least through the first half of next year,\" he said in the chip maker's third quarter earnings report.\nIn the earnings call, he said the firm had significantly ramped up investment in equipment in the third quarter and expected that to be \"even more significant\" in the following three months.",
